1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:06,380
English spelling is unreliable, so dictionaries describe sounds with phonetic symbols.

2
00:00:06,380 --> 00:00:14,153
You are not asked to transcribe, only to recognise the common symbols and hear the contrasts Nepali does not make.

3
00:00:14,153 --> 00:00:19,388
Theta, in think, often becomes an aspirated t: tink.

4
00:00:19,388 --> 00:00:22,903
Eth, in this, becomes a hard d: dis.

5
00:00:22,903 --> 00:00:25,468
V becomes w: wery.

6
00:00:25,468 --> 00:00:27,682
Z becomes j: joo.

7
00:00:27,682 --> 00:00:29,960
The vowel of bad drifts to bed.

8
00:00:29,960 --> 00:00:31,718
Bird gets a full r: burd.

9
00:00:31,718 --> 00:00:37,578
And the schwa, the weak vowel in about and teacher, disappears into a full vowel.

